    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Fathom is a San Francisco-based, for-profit public company (ticker: FTHM, CIK: 0001753162) founded in 2020. Its website describes the company as a provider of AI-powered meeting tools that capture, transcribe, and summarize calls on Zoom, Google Meet, and Microsoft Teams. The service is free for individuals, with additional team-oriented features including AI-powered CRM updates, AI Scorecards for real-time coaching and performance tracking, and automated action items that the company says flow directly into existing business tools.\n\nFathom's core product is its AI meeting notetaker, which the site also positions as a searchable record of past meetings through a feature called Ask Fathom, allowing users to query call content and generate customizable summaries. The product is registered in this site's catalog under the Notes, Knowledge and Meetings category, with noted capabilities covering auto-summaries, CRM sync, and consent and privacy handling. Fathom also maintains a listed MCP server, described as giving AI assistants real meeting context so that outputs are grounded in a user's actual work.",
